1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,853
Meet CredOrbit. Your cloud access, in
orbit.

2
00:00:04,173 --> 00:00:08,851
CredOrbit is one app for AWS IAM Identity
Center. It signs you in, discovers every

3
00:00:08,851 --> 00:00:13,530
account and role assigned to you, keeps
your AWS config in sync, and fetches

4
00:00:13,530 --> 00:00:18,208
temporary credentials, all from a single
terminal.

5
00:00:22,408 --> 00:00:26,336
It's a single static binary for macOS,
Linux and Windows. No AWS command line,

6
00:00:26,336 --> 00:00:30,265
Bash or Python required.

7
00:00:30,585 --> 00:00:33,680
Run CredOrbit, and the interactive
interface opens.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,396
The header always shows your sign-in
status, the active SSO session, and

9
00:00:37,396 --> 00:00:40,792
whether you're in normal or script-
compatible mode.

10
00:00:45,108 --> 00:00:48,413
Browse Accounts and Roles lists every
account assigned to you, discovered live

11
00:00:48,413 --> 00:00:51,719
from Identity Center. Nothing is hard-
coded.

12
00:00:52,039 --> 00:00:55,188
Search by name, account ID, or profile.

13
00:00:55,508 --> 00:00:58,545
Filter by environment, status or group,
and see at a glance when each account's

14
00:00:58,545 --> 00:01:01,581
credentials expire.

15
00:01:01,901 --> 00:01:04,689
Select accounts with the space bar to use
them in any operation, without changing

16
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:07,477
your saved groups.

17
00:01:11,808 --> 00:01:14,378
Your Main Accounts are the set you work
with every day.

18
00:01:14,698 --> 00:01:18,309
Toggle membership with the space bar, and
save with Ctrl+S.

19
00:01:18,629 --> 00:01:22,318
Groups are stored by stable account ID,
and removing an account from a group never

20
00:01:22,318 --> 00:01:26,008
deletes its AWS profile or credentials.

21
00:01:30,341 --> 00:01:33,489
Full Setup and Sync runs the whole
workflow in one pass.

22
00:01:33,809 --> 00:01:36,721
Choose the session, the mode, and the
account scope.

23
00:01:37,041 --> 00:01:39,821
CredOrbit signs in, discovers your
accounts, and compares them with your AWS

24
00:01:39,821 --> 00:01:42,600
config.

25
00:01:42,921 --> 00:01:46,327
Before anything is written, every change
is shown for your review.

26
00:01:46,647 --> 00:01:49,762
After you approve, credentials are fetched
in parallel and written atomically, with

27
00:01:49,762 --> 00:01:52,878
your files backed up first.

28
00:01:53,198 --> 00:01:56,013
The report shows exactly what happened:
what was exported, what failed, and where

29
00:01:56,013 --> 00:01:58,829
the backups are.

30
00:02:03,141 --> 00:02:06,025
If you use Claude Code with Amazon
Bedrock, CredOrbit rotates the AWS account

31
00:02:06,025 --> 00:02:08,909
it uses.

32
00:02:09,228 --> 00:02:12,060
It only picks accounts with valid
credentials, and never repeats the current

33
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:14,891
one when there's an alternative.

34
00:02:19,191 --> 00:02:22,839
And when something is wrong, Diagnostics
checks your SSO sessions, TLS and

35
00:02:22,839 --> 00:02:26,487
corporate certificates, file permissions,
and the Claude integration, with a clear

36
00:02:26,487 --> 00:02:30,135
fix for every issue.

37
00:02:32,234 --> 00:02:35,269
CredOrbit is free for personal,
educational and non-profit use. Companies

38
00:02:35,269 --> 00:02:38,304
need a commercial license.

39
00:02:38,624 --> 00:02:42,185
Install it with go install, or download a
release from GitHub.

40
00:02:42,505 --> 00:02:45,208
CredOrbit. Your cloud access, in orbit.

